ompress and/or Snappy.getNativeLibraryVersion()) instead of asserting the old boolean return. Separately, snappy-java bundles per-OS/arch JNI libraries inside the jar under org/xerial/snappy/native/<os>/<arch>/; this is NOT part of the normal generated scaffold. Preserve the existing build.gradle's extractSnappyNativeLibrary Copy task, the `-Djava.library.path=<extracted dir>` and `--add-opens=java.base/java.lang=ALL-UNNAMED` test jvmArgs, and the matching `--add-opens` native-image buildArg — the resource layout is unchanged in 1.1.0.1 so this logic carries over unmodified.\",\n  \"risks\": [\"If the fix only patches the two isNativeLibraryLoaded() call sites without re-running compileTestJava, other now-removed/renamed SnappyLoader members used elsewhere in the test could still surface later, though none were found in this pass.\"]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":9881,"type":"result","duration_ms":95230,"uuid":"5c01dc2c-8128-4d29-9435-c71067c6d7d2","ttft_stream_ms":914,"time_to_request_ms":57,"first_content_frame_ms":914,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

